From d312a60a67631843769910ea63fb40c926bf72a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:10:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Split Valithria's adds between the tanks and kill them in
 order

Playerbots.ValithriaAdds and Playerbots.ValithriaPortalTurns (both default 1).

With 0021 the dojo 10-heroic raid lost both tanks at 161-206 s. The warrior held every zombie that the
skull and the stock tank pick sent him (195-202k of zombie melee), Gut Spray landed on everyone in front
of an abomination (the dream-cloud multiplier blocked tank face), worms piled on whichever tank stood
nearest, the skull waited on archmages while a skeleton's Lay Waste burned the whole room (up to 394k
raid damage), half the Frostbolt Volleys landed (202k) and neither tank used a defensive cooldown in
the whole pull.

- In a 10-player raid the bot tanks split her adds (RaidInteractions::VdwTankHolds): only bot tanks
  alive and within 80 yd of her heal spot are ranked (VdwRankTanks; a human, self-bot, dead or far
  tank holds nothing, and a tank outside the ranking tanks as in 0021; an add on such a tank stays
  there, as 0021 left every add on a tank). The first by guid holds the
  abominations, the second the archmages, skeletons and blistering zombies (a heroic zombie one-shot a
  kiting damage dealer), both share the rot worms, a tank taking another stray worm only while it
  holds no more than the other; a lone ranked tank holds them all. A tank picks up only adds within
  the 45 yd marking radius (one that went out to the doors held a skeleton 60-65 yd away, out of the
  skull's reach, for 50 s of Lay Waste). A ranked tank's own target leaves out what it does not hold
  unless it is on it, and every suppresser (RaidIccStrategy::AppendTargetExclusions).
- Tank face runs for a ranked tank on an abomination, so its Gut Spray points away from the raid.
- One skull in kill order (VdwKillRank, 10-player): skeleton, zombie, rot worms, suppressers,
  archmages, a lone abomination last (with two up, one of them right after the worms: last in line,
  the first lived 122 s and two sat on the abomination tank for 60 s); worms and suppressers are
  marked where the most stand, so area spells hit the pile; a mark moves only to a more urgent kind.
  Melee never takes a zombie: while the skull is one it fights the best melee target nearest to
  itself and at least 15 yd from any zombie (picked by the distance from the zombie, it walked into
  the zombie rule and turned back).
- icc valithria interrupt (ACTION_RAID + 6): warriors, rogues, mages, shamans, hunters and death
  knights interrupt the nearest Frostbolt Volley in reach.
- icc valithria tank cooldown (ACTION_EMERGENCY + 1): Shield Block, Shield Wall, Last Stand; Divine
  Protection, Lay on Hands; Vampiric Blood, Icebound Fortitude; Barkskin, Survival Instincts, each
  below its health line (stock Shield Wall sat at ACTION_MEDIUM_HEAL, under the rotation). Both
  triggers wait for her encounter (valithria_watch engaged) before any search, and both run in any
  raid size.
- No crowd control on a zombie a ranked tank holds.
- ValithriaPortalTurns, on 10-player heroic: the bot healers on her take the Nightmare portals one at
  a time. Live on 2026-11-26 both went through every wave together (portal=2, then dream=2), leaving
  one or none healing her for 20-25 s a cycle. On normal they still all go: the Dream clouds hurt
  nobody and their Emerald Vigor is the healing engine (with turns the dojo 10-normal raid peaked at
  8-10 stacks instead of 18-38 and lost her at 96%); 25-player keeps 0021's portals. At most one
  healer is in the dream or holds a live portal claim: any group member in the dream, a human or the
  raid healer included, holds it. Never so many go that fewer than one (two with four or more
  healers) stay on her, and the turn goes to the free bot healer with the fewest trips, then the
  oldest trip (RaidInteractions::TakesPortalTurn). Human healers are never ranked (they record no
  trips and would hold the turn forever) but count toward the floor while on her; a healer a zombie
  or worm chases, or below half health, is passed over. A healer back from a heroic dream carries
  Twisted Nightmares for 40 s (200 Nature a second per stack, 43-146k per healer per dojo pull, the
  largest damage either took; Columns of Frost then finished them): it heals itself first while below
  70% with any stack (below 50% too: the heal trigger fires there for such a carrier), steps out of a
  Mana Void even while stacked, and the walk to a
  portal steps out of Columns and Voids (the portal action outranked the group action's sidestep).
- valithria_watch gains adds= and turns= (also on its end line).
- Both switches at 0 restore the 0021 behaviour exactly. ValithriaAdds = 0 alone still takes heroic
  portals in turns; ValithriaPortalTurns = 0 alone sends the healers on her through each heroic wave
  together, as 0021 does.
