--- a/conf/playerbots.conf.dist
+++ b/conf/playerbots.conf.dist
@@ -503,6 +503,28 @@ Playerbots.ValithriaHealerFocus = 1
 # hurting her. 0 keeps every healer out of the dream. Default: 1.
 Playerbots.ValithriaPortals = 1
 
+# Icecrown Citadel, Valithria Dreamwalker: her adds. In a 10-player raid the bot tanks within reach of her split
+# them: the first holds the abominations and faces their Gut Spray away from the raid; the second holds the
+# archmages, skeletons and blistering zombies; both share the rot worms (a lone bot tank, or one whose partner is a
+# human, dead or far away, holds them all). There the damage dealers kill a skeleton first, then a zombie, the
+# worms, the suppressers, the archmages and a lone abomination last (with two up, one goes right after the worms),
+# with worms and suppressers marked where the most stand. In any raid size a bot with an interrupt stops a Frostbolt
+# Volley and a tank under her adds uses its own defensive cooldowns; a 25-player raid otherwise tanks and marks as
+# before. 0 turns all of this off. Only this and ValithriaPortalTurns both at 0 restore the ValithriaHealerFocus
+# behaviour exactly. Default: 1.
+Playerbots.ValithriaAdds = 1
+
+# With ValithriaPortals, in a 10-player heroic raid: the bot healers on her take the Nightmare portals in turn. At
+# most one healer (a bot or a human) is in the dream or on the way to a portal at a time, never so many that fewer
+# than one (two with four or more healers) stay on her, and the turn goes to the free bot healer with the fewest
+# trips; one a zombie or worm chases, or below half health, is passed over. A human healer takes his own portals and
+# is never given a turn. On normal they all go (Emerald Vigor stacks are the healing engine there), and a 25-player
+# raid keeps the earlier portals. A healer back from a heroic dream with Twisted Nightmares heals itself first below
+# 70% and steps out of Mana Voids even while stacked; the walk to a portal steps out of Columns of Frost and Mana
+# Voids. 0 sends every healer on her through each heroic wave together, as before. Only this and ValithriaAdds both
+# at 0 restore the ValithriaHealerFocus behaviour exactly. Default: 1.
+Playerbots.ValithriaPortalTurns = 1
+
 # Opt-in Malygos drake positioning/rotation and human-led Flame Leviathan vehicles.
 # Uses normal boarding and spell costs; never moves the human or skips a boss.
 Playerbots.RaidVehicleSupport = 0
